Yes, I agree:  that would be unbalanced.  The Eye
is sufficiently compelling as it stands, and indeed
would be worth an artifact wish for many neutral
characters even without the branchport capability.

There are quest artifacts that could stand to be
beefed up, to make them more worthwhile.  I believe
I previously mentioned that I don't bother to carry
the Heart out of the Barbarian quest.  Why would
I carry a luckstone that the Wizard will specifically
target and steal, which isn't already blessed?  I
wouldn't, given that by that point in the game I 
already have a blessed luckstone from Mine's End.
You don't need an artifact for stealth, because 
that's easy to obtain in other ways just in general
and also because Barbarians in particular get it
for free at XL15.  The double damage when slung
is meaningless for a single projectile that has
to be retrieved before it can be used again.  

That leaves levitation.  Admittedly, if you haven't
got a ring or boots of levitation, the Heart's 
toggle-able version would be preferable to using 
potions.  I suppose if I reached the Medusa level
as a Barbarian and had not yet obtained the ring 
or boots or a wand of polymorph, I'd probably go 
fetch the Heart and use it for levitation until I 
reached the Castle.

Still, for a quest artifact, that's pretty seriously
underpowered.  The only circumstances where I can
imagine anyone wishing for it involve the desire
to have useless artifacts, either for goofy bragging
rights on ascension or to leave weird bones.  In such
cases I'd also expect to see the same player collecting
the likes of Dragonbane, Grimtooth, Ogresmasher, etc.
If I were rebalancing NetHack, the Barbarian role
would get a new quest artifact.

